invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_test
reason: srv_ext_over_max answers 1 only past SRV_CLIENT_HELLO_EXT_MAX + 1
  extensions, so the parser accepts a ClientHello of 129, one past the
  bound srv_parser.h states (docs/decisions.md 59). This is the upper side
  of the boundary pair: test/srv_parser_reader_tests.h fills the golden
  hello out to one past the bound and requires illegal_parameter.

--- old
        if (count > SRV_CLIENT_HELLO_EXT_MAX) {
--- new
        if (count > SRV_CLIENT_HELLO_EXT_MAX + 1) {
